# Backend integration rules

## LHOS agent server (the "computer")
- Base URL: env `LHOS_BASE_URL` (prod: `https://mcp.hostx.h22t.com`).
- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer ${LHOS_MCP_TOKEN}` (env; set by scripts/sync-env.sh).
- REST surface (full detail: docs/API_REFERENCE.md):
  - `GET  /api/tools` → tool catalog `[{name, description, input_schema}]`
  - `POST /api/tools/<name>` → execute tool, JSON body = args
  - `GET  /api/capabilities` | `/api/events?date=&limit=` | `/api/report?date=` | `/api/approvals`
- MCP endpoint `POST /mcp` (Streamable HTTP, same bearer) — used by the orchestrator
  loop via `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` client. Prefer REST for dashboard data,
  MCP for the agent loop.
- All LHOS calls go through one typed client: `src/server/lhos/client.ts`
  (timeouts, retries on 5xx only, zod-parsed responses, usage/latency logging).
- Tool results can contain base64 images — persist to `files` table + object dir,
  pass URLs to the UI, never inline megabytes into chat state.

## Model vendors (orchestrator brains)
- Registry: `config/models.json` (OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter). Keys from env only:
  `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.
- One adapter interface `ModelAdapter` (stream, toolCall, countUsage) per vendor in
  `src/server/models/*`; selection + per-model pricing comes from the registry.
- Every completion writes a `usage_events` row (tokens in/out, cached, cost USD,
  vendor, model, chat_id, purpose) — the live billing ticker reads this via SSE.

## Agent orchestration
- The agent loop runs **server-side** (`src/server/agent/loop.ts`): plan → tool call
  (LHOS MCP) → observe → repeat, streaming step events to the client over SSE.
- Steps are persisted (`runs`, `run_steps`) so a refresh reattaches to a live run.
- Approval checkpoints: when LHOS returns `awaiting_approval` or policy requires it,
  pause the run, emit `approval_required`, resume only after owner action.
- Takeover: `request_takeover` → surface the embedded VNC panel immediately.
